      "start_seconds": 316.09,
      "end_seconds": 319.27,
      "duration_seconds": 3.18,
      "text": "Let me examine it won't take long."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 320.56,
      "end_seconds": 321.26,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Sure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 322.15,
      "end_seconds": 324.32,
      "duration_seconds": 2.17,
      "text": "Just relax, I'll be quick."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 341.43,
      "end_seconds": 348.78,
      "duration_seconds": 7.35,
      "text": "Grouped blisters on a red base along one rib on the left not crossing the midline"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 353.61,
      "end_seconds": 376.8,
      "duration_seconds": 23.19,
      "text": "Okay, finished. Right, here's what I'm thinking. I think we're dealing with shingles at this stage. An insect-bite reaction is still possible. Let me just check I've got this right. You've had itching for five days, severe, and no immune problems or rash on the face."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 378.33,
      "end_seconds": 379.03,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "exactly"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 379.69,
      "end_seconds": 402.06,
      "duration_seconds": 22.37,
      "text": "I'll start you on aciclovir, 800 milligrams, five times a day, for seven days. That should help with shingles. It's a commonly used medicine and most people tolerate it well. Keep the blisters clean and covered, and avoid contact with anyone pregnant or newborn until they crust. Okay, we're done for today. Take care."
    },
